          "normalized_summary": "A new study provides a blueprint for the next generation of antivenoms by using snakes’ natural molecular defenses against their own deadly venom. Venomous snakes carry their own antidotes. Proteins circulating in their blood can block the toxins they produce, protecting the animals from accidental exposure to their own venom. University of Maryland researchers have [...]",
